## Admin Features

### Accessing Admin Dashboard
1. Login with staff/admin credentials
2. Click **"Dashboard"** in navigation (staff only)

### Admin Dashboard Sections

#### Statistics Overview
- Total conversions across all users
- Total revenue generated
- Total revision materials
- Total downloads

#### Weekly Performance
- Daily conversion activity
- Payment transactions
- Revenue per day

#### Recent Activity
- Latest conversions
- Payment records
- Failed conversions

#### Attention Needed
- Pending payments
- Failed conversions
- Issues requiring action

#### Quick Actions
- Manage subscription plans
- Upload revision materials
- Add subjects
- View all materials
- Access Django Admin

### Django Admin Panel

#### Managing Subscription Plans
1. Go to **Django Admin** (http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/)
2. Click **"Subscription plans"**
3. Click **"Add subscription plan"**
4. Fill in details:
   - **Name**: Plan name (e.g., "School Premium")
   - **Plan Type**: Basic/Standard/Premium
   - **Plan Target**: Individual/School/Both
   - **Duration**: Per Term or Per Year
   - **Amount**: Price in KSH
   - **Features**: Check what's included
   - **Limits**: Max teachers/classes (0 = unlimited)
5. Click **"Save"**

#### Managing Revision Materials
1. In Django Admin, click **"Revision materials"**
2. Click **"Add revision material"**
3. Fill in details:
   - **Title**: Material name
   - **Subject**: Select subject
   - **Type**: Past Paper/Marking Scheme/Notes/Textbook
   - **Term**: Term 1/2/3
   - **Year**: Academic year
   - **Price**: Free or paid amount
   - **File**: Upload the document
4. Click **"Save"**

#### Linking Materials
- Link past papers to their marking schemes
- Go to **"Link Materials"** in revision admin
- Select past paper and marking scheme
- Click **"Link"**

